<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17270" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exstructĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">extr-</span></b> ),
		ōnis, f.
		exstruo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a building up</i>, <i>erecting</i>,
				<i>structure.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop. (rare but class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tectorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D. 2, 60, 150</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">contecti eā exstructione, quae sit ad
					memoriam aeternitatis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Phil. 14, 13, 34</span></i>
			. —With <i>gen.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vallorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Ezech. 17, 17</span></i>
			.—In plur.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fastigiorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 7,
					1 <i>med.</i></span></i>
			 —* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>an adorning</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Tert. ad Uxor. 2, 3</span></i>.</div>
